  2 |     """
  3 |     Given a positive integer n, return a sorted list that has the odd numbers in collatz sequence.
  4 | 
  5 |     The Collatz conjecture is a conjecture in mathematics that concerns a sequence defined
  6 |     as follows: start with any positive integer n. Then each term is obtained from the 
  7 |     previous term as follows: if the previous term is even, the next term is one half of 
  8 |     the previous term. If the previous term is odd, the next term is 3 times the previous
  9 |     term plus 1. The conjecture is that no matter what value of n, the sequence will always reach 1.
